{"resourceIdentifier":"3868","resourceName":"Fangchenggang Mangrove afforestation project","description":"Fangchenggang Mangrove Afforestation Project is located in Gangkou District and Fangcheng District of Fangchenggang City, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China. The purpose of the project is to increase carbon sequestration and contribute to local sustainable development by planting mangroves in degraded mangrove habitats. The project proponent is Fangchenggang Xinggang Agricultural Development Co., Ltd.The purpose of the project is to restore the degraded local mangrove ecosystem and increase forest cover by planting a variety of species of native mangrove, and establish a healthy local ecological and economic system by involving residents in the implementation of the projects directly. Totally 221.9 ha of mangroves have been planted with 5 native mangrove species (such as Avicennia marina, Kandelia candel, Aegiceras corniculatum, Rhizophora stylosa, Bruguiera gymnorrhiza). The implementation of the afforestation project will generate GHG emission removals, improve the local environment, enhance the capabilities of local communities and residents by providing them with relevant technical skills. In addition, the project has restored the degraded mangrove ecosystem and increased forest coverage, provided a suitable habitat for animals, especially for endangered birds which mainly live in mangroves. The project is estimated to generate GHG emission removals of 111,592 tCO2e in 40 years, with an average annual GHG emission removal of 2,789.8tCO2e.","location":{"latitude":21.668995,"longitude":108.345666},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-05-07","endExclusive":"2024-06-07","endInclusive":"2024-06-06"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3868"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guangxi"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"cod